  "stem": "A mixing bowl is shaped like a hemisphere (half of a sphere) with a radius of 6 inches. The volume of the bowl is \\(k\\pi\\) cubic inches. What is the value of \\(k\\)?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "spr",
  "choices": null,
  "answer": null,
  "spr_answers": [
    "144"
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Volume of a full sphere: \\(\\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^{3} = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi(6^{3}) = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi(216) = 288\\pi\\).",
    "A hemisphere is half of that: \\(144\\pi\\). So \\(k = 144\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": null,
  "traps": null,
  "verify": "ans=(Rational(1,2)*Rational(4,3)*pi*6**3)/pi\nassert ans==144\nassert Rational(spr_answers[0])==ans\n",
